{"name":"Monogram","hex":"#595747","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"monogram","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A picture drawn in line only, before the colour and/or shading is applied; an outline sketch."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A sentence consisting of only one line, or an epigram consisting of only one verse, of poetry."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/monogram"}],"entries":[{"title":"Monogram","blocks":[{"text":"A monogram is a motif made by overlapping or combining two or more letters or other graphemes to form one symbol. Monograms are often made by combining the initials of an individual or a company, used as recognizable symbols or logos. A series of uncombined initials is properly referred to as a cypher and is not a monogram."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monogram","wikidata":"Q168346"},{"title":"Monogram (company)","blocks":[{"text":"Mattel acquired Monogram in 1968, and the firm passed through various owners and was merged with Revell, the combined company being bought by Hobbico in 2007. Along with Revell, AMT, and MPC, Monogram is sometimes called one of the traditional \"Big 4\" in plastic modeling."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5d/Monogram_modelbrand_logo.png/330px-Monogram_modelbrand_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monogram_(company)","wikidata":"Q11344441"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Sarcophage_de_Drausin_03_chrisme.jpg/250px-Sarcophage_de_Drausin_03_chrisme.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Sarcophage_de_Drausin_03_chrisme.jpg/500px-Sarcophage_de_Drausin_03_chrisme.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Sar